        <section id="buying-guide" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f8fafc,#eff6ff);border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:24px;padding:clamp(20px,4vw,38px);margin:10px 0 34px;">
            <h2 style="font-size:34px;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 15px;font-weight:900;">How to Choose the Right Headphones</h2>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">1. Start with the listening environment</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">For flights, trains and noisy offices, prioritize active noise cancelling headphones such as Soundcore Space 2, Raycon Everyday or Edifier W800BT Pro. For outdoor running and cycling, open-ear headphones may be safer because they preserve awareness. For a quiet home studio, a wired monitoring model can be more reliable than Bluetooth.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">2. Choose between over-ear, on-ear and in-ear designs</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">Over-ear headphones surround the ear and are often the most comfortable for long sessions. On-ear headphones are smaller but may apply more pressure. In-ear wireless earbuds are compact and convenient for movement, while earhooks improve stability during workouts.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">3. Understand active noise cancellation versus isolation</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">Active noise cancellation uses microphones and electronic processing to reduce continuous environmental noise. Passive isolation relies on the physical seal of cushions or ear tips. ANC is especially useful for engine rumble and office noise, while isolation may be sufficient for school, home and studio use.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">4. Compare real battery behavior</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">Battery claims may differ depending on volume, ANC use and connection mode. For earbuds, distinguish between per-charge runtime and total runtime with the case. Fast charging can be more useful than an extremely high maximum figure when headphones are used every day.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">5. Match connectivity to your devices</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">Check whether you need Bluetooth, a 3.5 mm jack, USB-C digital audio, USB-A, a 6.35 mm studio plug, Optical or RCA. Multipoint Bluetooth is useful for switching between a computer and phone. Wired connections remain valuable for studios, school computers, televisions and situations where latency matters.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">6. Evaluate microphone requirements</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">A built-in microphone is adequate for occasional calls, but professional meetings benefit from a boom microphone and dedicated noise reduction. The Logitech Zone 750 is more call-focused than lifestyle headphones because its microphone, controls and software are designed for office communication.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">7. Consider water resistance carefully</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">IPX4 and IPX5 ratings generally suit sweat and light moisture, while IPX7 products offer stronger protection. Water resistance does not automatically make a product suitable for swimming. Always follow the manufacturer’s limits.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:23px;color:#0f172a;margin:25px 0 9px;">8. Do not buy only by rating</h3>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:#334155;margin:0;">A high rating with a small number of reviews should be interpreted differently from a slightly lower rating backed by tens of thousands of reviews. Review volume, product age, use case and feature fit all matter. Ratings are a useful signal, not a substitute for evaluating specifications.</p>
        </section>

        <section itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage" id="faq" style="margin-bottom:34px;">
            <h2 style="font-size:34px;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 15px;font-weight:900;">Frequently Asked Questions About the Best Headphones</h2>
            <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">What are the best headphones for most people?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">For most buyers, the best headphones balance comfort, sound quality, battery life, microphone performance and the right type of noise control. In this guide, Soundcore Space 2 is the premium all-round travel choice, while Edifier W800BT Pro and BERIBES provide stronger value at lower prices.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">Are over-ear headphones better than wireless earbuds?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">Over-ear headphones usually provide larger drivers, longer battery life and greater comfort for extended listening. Wireless earbuds are smaller, easier to carry and often better for exercise. The better choice depends on whether you value immersion and battery life or compact portability.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">Which headphones are best for airplane travel?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">Travelers should prioritize active noise cancellation, comfortable over-ear cushions, long battery life and a wired fallback. Soundcore Space 2 is the strongest travel-focused option in this comparison, with up to 50 hours using ANC and up to 70 hours without it.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">Which are the best budget noise cancelling headphones?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">The Edifier W800BT Pro is the most feature-rich budget ANC model here. It combines advertised -44 dB hybrid ANC, Bluetooth 5.4, multipoint connection, USB-C digital audio, app EQ and fast charging.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">What are the best headphones for working out?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">PocBuds T60 are the strongest conventional workout earbuds because their earhooks improve stability and IPX7 protection helps with sweat and rain. CXK X13 is better for outdoor runners and cyclists who need an open-ear design to remain aware of traffic.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">Which headphones are best for studio recording?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">The OneOdio A71 is the dedicated studio-oriented option in this list. It uses a wired connection, 3.5 mm and 6.35 mm plugs, swiveling earcups and SharePort, making it suitable for home recording, DJ monitoring and instruments.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">What headphones are suitable for online meetings and office calls?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">The Logitech Zone 750 is the most work-focused headset because it has a noise-cancelling boom microphone, USB-C connection, USB-A adapter, inline call controls and Logi Tune software. Raycon, Soundcore and Edifier are more versatile wireless alternatives.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">Should children use volume-limited headphones?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">Volume-limited headphones can help reduce the risk of excessively high playback levels, but parents should still supervise listening volume and duration. The Monster Cute SK100 offers selectable 85/94 dB limits and is designed for children ages 3 to 12.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">Do wireless TV headphones reduce lip-sync delay?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">A dedicated 2.4 GHz TV system can provide lower and more predictable latency than ordinary Bluetooth. The NUBWO HT02 is specified below 20 ms and includes Optical, RCA and AUX inputs plus a charging transmitter base.</p></div>
            </div><div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:16px;padding:18px;margin-bottom:12px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 9px;">How often should this headphone guide be updated?</h3>
                <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p itemprop="text" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#475569;margin:0;">Prices, availability, product revisions and ratings change frequently. A commercial comparison should be reviewed every 60 to 90 days, with price claims rechecked before publication and a visible updated date added to the page.</p></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a,#1e3a8a);border-radius:24px;padding:clamp(22px,4vw,40px);color:#fff;margin-bottom:20px;">
